<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{% block title %}Potentially Beautiful Views of England{% endblock %}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{% block description %}Objective, terrain-computed discovery of panoramic viewpoints in England{% endblock %}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ root }}assets/style.css">
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 viewBox=%220 0 100 100%22><text y=%22.9em%22 font-size=%2290%22>&#x26F0;</text></svg>">
{% block head %}{% endblock %}
</head>
<body>
<header class="site">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="{{ root }}index.html">Potentially Beautiful <span>Views of England</span></a>
    <nav>
      <a href="{{ root }}index.html">Map &amp; rankings</a>
      <a href="{{ root }}postcode.html">Near me</a>
      <a href="{{ root }}vote.html">Vote</a>
      <a href="{{ root }}verification.html">Verification</a>
      <a href="{{ root }}methodology.html">Methodology</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/vassiliphilippov/england-pbv">GitHub</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>
<main class="wrap">
{% block content %}{% endblock %}
</main>
<footer class="site">
  <div class="wrap">
    Computed from open data: OS Terrain 50 (contains OS data &copy; Crown copyright and database right 2026)
    &middot; ESA WorldCover 2021 (CC-BY 4.0) &middot; OpenStreetMap (ODbL) &middot; Database of British and Irish Hills (CC-BY 4.0)
    &middot; Environment Agency LiDAR Composite DTM (OGL) &middot; Natural England Priority Habitats Inventory and CRoW Access Layer (OGL)
    &middot; renders contain modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2023&ndash;2026 (CC BY-SA 3.0 IGO).
    Scores describe measurable view geometry ("view potential"), never beauty itself.
    Locations are computed &mdash; always check access rights, paths and safety before visiting.
  </div>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
